{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1289284-unawakened-flaw-can-t-find-it","id":1289284,"title":"\"Unawakened\" Flaw - can't find it","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-18T13:16:01-08:00","id":1289284,"title":"\"Unawakened\" Flaw - can't find it","content":"I remember reading a flaw which said you have no arete, no spheres, and are limited to what your other traits give you. You can have certain Wonders and Backgrounds, but you won't be using Magick. &quot;Just take your freebies and don't try and be a Weretiger or something&quot;.<br /> <br /> I can't find it anywhere; does anyone know what flaw I'm talking about? I'm guessing there have been multiple versions of it across old books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T00:03:47-08:00","id":1289438,"title":"","content":"May have been in Ascension's Right hand - that was the book for assistants and consors and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T03:25:13-08:00","id":1289456,"title":"","content":"Sounds like the soulless flaw from guide to the technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T05:40:30-08:00","id":1289481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1289284-unawakened-flaw-can-t-find-it#post1289284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember reading a flaw which said you have no arete, no spheres, and are limited to what your other traits give you. You can have certain Wonders and Backgrounds, but you won't be using Magick. &quot;Just take your freebies and don't try and be a Weretiger or something&quot;.<br /> <br /> I can't find it anywhere; does anyone know what flaw I'm talking about? I'm guessing there have been multiple versions of it across old books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that called &quot;being a regular person&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6470-sardonis","name":"Sardonis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T06:45:05-08:00","id":1289493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sardonis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1289284-unawakened-flaw-can-t-find-it?p=1289481#post1289481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that called &quot;being a regular person&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh...the common Flaw of not being a Mage. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sorry, I don't remember that Flaw. If my memory doesn't fail, human Consors start with 21 freebies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T07:16:32-08:00","id":1289511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1289284-unawakened-flaw-can-t-find-it?p=1289493#post1289493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh...the common Flaw of not being a Mage. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sorry, I don't remember that Flaw. If my memory doesn't fail, human Consors start with 21 freebies</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I find that Unawakenedist!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6470-sardonis","name":"Sardonis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T13:53:32-08:00","id":1289639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sardonis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1289284-unawakened-flaw-can-t-find-it?p=1289481#post1289481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that called &quot;being a regular person&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well not exactly; it's presented in a context of &quot;you might own a Wonder or have Enhancements&quot;, and the idea is that you're choosing to play a mortal among Mages, not a regular everyday mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T18:02:06-08:00","id":1290164,"title":"","content":"The closest I've seen for this is Struggling Awake, a 5-point Merit that gives a Sorcerer limited access to Awakened Magick. But I don't think an \u201cUnawakened\u201d Flaw exists. It didn't make sense: taking a Flaw because you're a mortal with Backgrounds that mortals normally don't have? How is that a Flaw?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T18:16:48-08:00","id":1290170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1289284-unawakened-flaw-can-t-find-it?p=1290164#post1290164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The closest I've seen for this is Struggling Awake, a 5-point Merit that gives a Sorcerer limited access to Awakened Magick. But I don't think an \u201cUnawakened\u201d Flaw exists. It didn't make sense: taking a Flaw because you're a mortal with Backgrounds that mortals normally don't have? How is that a Flaw?</div> </div> </div> </div>I found it! It's a flaw in the Technocracy Revised book intended for PCs who are playing things like Hit Marks. And mortals can have Enhancements, there's nothing magickal about possessing them. Same goes for plenty of Wonders, and even arguably some things like Dream and Demesne. None of these things have Sphere prerequisites or demand that you're a Mage (well some Wonders do).<br /> <br /> It's 7 points and raises the max freebie total to 21, 7 higher than normal. You're meant to be a powerful non-magickal ally who the other PCs can work off of essentially, it's very far from playing a &quot;mortal&quot; PC. It's a flaw in the sense that you lose a free dot of Arete (worth 4 freebies right?) and 6 dots of Spheres (worth 7 each for a total of 42 freebies), and place yourself on a very linear power progression vs other characters who are more exponential. The big upside is that in a collaborative game with little PC conflict that won't matter since PCs can apply their buffs to you, the perfect damage-resistant combat-blender canvas for their effects. Furthermore, any PC who can create charms or wonders, if given enough time and quintessence, can give you the ability to work &quot;magick&quot;. It's probably underpowered overall but definitely interesting.<br /> <br /> For example you could play an Enhancements 5, Hypercram 5 cyborg with plenty of dots invested in Advantages for extra soak. The Hypercram is justified by the &quot;online access&quot; enhancement and a body/mind designed to integrate data into muscle memory. For the sake of balance such a PC couldn't awaken or learn sorcery, or anything along those lines. Many Mage PCs place their freebies into Avatar, Spheres and Arete so such a PC would probably have better Abilities overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-20-2019, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T19:08:22-08:00","id":1290200,"title":"","content":"You mean Soulless? That's a bit more than \u201cyou have Arete 0\u201d; it's \u201cyou don't have a soul\u201d.<br /> <br /> And for what it's worth, <b>Gods and Monsters</b> addresses unEnlightened Technocrats \u2014 <i>without</i> the Soulless Flaw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-20-2019, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T04:34:36-08:00","id":1290296,"title":"","content":"Yup, It doesn't mean you're a &quot;mortal among mages&quot;. It means you don't have an Avatar, which it's everything but normal. In fact, you're not a &quot;Sleeper&quot;, because that would imply having a sleeping Avatar...which you don't have. That's why it's common in artificial constructs like Hit-Marks.<br /> <br /> Mortals among mages (Consors) also tend to receive more freebies, but they don't need to be Soulless","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T10:56:00-08:00","id":1290430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1289284-unawakened-flaw-can-t-find-it?p=1290296#post1290296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup, It doesn't mean you're a &quot;mortal among mages&quot;. It means you don't have an Avatar, which it's everything but normal. In fact, you're not a &quot;Sleeper&quot;, because that would imply having a sleeping Avatar...which you don't have. That's why it's common in artificial constructs like Hit-Marks.<br /> <br /> Mortals among mages (Consors) also tend to receive more freebies, but they don't need to be Soulless</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh interesting. It would be interesting to see a Technephandi who was pushing for the Union to gradually replace the masses with Soulless beings. That would give them ultimate control over reality, is the argument, since the Masses would be compliant. You need to a be a Sleeper to contribute to Consensus after all. The real aim is to do Nephandic shit of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T07:04:43-08:00","id":1290748,"title":"","content":"That would be an interesting plot. It certainly follows a Nephandic agenda<br /> <br /> Also, I think that this way to weaken the foundations of reality could be controvertial within the ranks of the Fallen themselves: Many fallen believe their duty to corrupt souls and invert Avatars. And nobody knows what Avatars do between reincarnations. From a certain PoV, less Avatars to corrupt makes the job easier, but from another those Avatars that aren't in the world are still there, doing who knows what.<br /> <br /> Since Avatar reproduction it's a mystery, a Nephandus could believe that having less people with &quot;shards of the one&quot; imply that those shards that are left will join into stronger Avatars (this would be compatible with the Euthanatos view of life as a finite resource). An Infernalist Nephandi may resent that more souless people means less souls for their demonic alies. And what if the process interferes with the reincarnation of Widderslainte, as there are less able bodies?. Nephandy don't have all the answers...but they sure have lot's of evil plans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-22-2019, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T17:58:47-07:00","id":1404852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1289284-unawakened-flaw-can-t-find-it?p=1290430#post1290430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh interesting. It would be interesting to see a Technephandi who was pushing for the Union to gradually replace the masses with Soulless beings. That would give them ultimate control over reality, is the argument, since the Masses would be compliant. You need to a be a Sleeper to contribute to Consensus after all. The real aim is to do Nephandic shit of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Has flashbacks to reading 1e Progenitors*<br /> <br /> Well, that scheme involved Avatar-killing drugs in the water supply, but it's functionally identical and suffers from the same flaw; &quot;replacing the masses with Soulless beings&quot; takes away a great deal of the Technocracy's power, which is founded in the influence they possess over Consensus. It would level the playing field vastly in favour of the Traditions. That's not to stop it being the pet project of some crazed Master who the others look at cautiously though - this was what the thing in Progenitors 1e was eventually retconned as - or indeed, a scheme by a Progenitor <i>Barabbus</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 07-26-2020, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}